  set:  # e07b
    title: "kotlin: a method call whose receiver is not a bare identifier, 'this' or a call (a.b.m(), a fully-qualified inline call, \"x\".m(), (x).m(), xs[0].m(), super.m()) emits NO calls edge"  # e07b
    fields:  # e07b
      statement: "Every Kotlin call site the analyzer parses must emit a calls edge, resolved or unresolved, whatever the syntactic shape of its receiver. VIOLATED: a receiver that is a navigation chain not rooted at 'this' (h.file.readText(), System.out.println, java.nio.file.Files.readAllBytes(p) written inline), a literal, a parenthesized or index expression, or super emits nothing. Filed instance: the inline fully-qualified call, which yields confirmed_with_caveats on a must_not_exist fs_read claim that names no caveat about the read."  # e07b
      root_cause: "kotlin.py's navigation-receiver loop (~1462) keeps a receiver only if it is this_expression, navigation_expression, call_expression or identifier. A navigation_expression receiver is handled only in Case 1b (rooted at this), and the unresolved-edge fallback (~1740) is inside the final else branch that a nav receiver never reaches. Any other receiver node type is skipped, so the METHOD identifier is taken as the receiver, method_node stays None, and nothing is emitted."  # e07b
- op: discuss  # 1b9e
