  message: "RE-VERIFIED AND RE-SCOPED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081 (filed yesterday by me; the root cause was left undetermined and is now read). Record: scratchpad dupol/.\n\n1. THE FILED INSTANCE REPRODUCES, AND IT IS A CLEAN VERDICT. The filing did not run whether the missing edge yields a false 'confirmed'. It does, once the repo has any other edge:\n     fun helper(s: String) = s.trim()\n     fun readInline(p: String) = java.nio.file.Files.readAllBytes(java.nio.file.Paths.get(helper(p)))\n   must_not_exist fs_read  -> confirmed_with_caveats. The ONLY caveat is unknown_receiver_scope naming 'trim'; readAllBytes is named nowhere.\n   Same for java.lang.System.getenv(...) inline on env_read.\n   With no other call in the repo the verdict is inconclusive, but only through the zero-edges guard ('the analysis produced no call edges at all').\n   Controls: the imported form is violated; java.net.URL(u).openStream() is violated (a call receiver is handled).\n\n2. ROOT CAUSE, read in kotlin.py's call arm (~1462-1790). The navigation-expression receiver loop keeps a receiver only if it is this_expression, navigation_expression, call_expression or identifier. Then:\n   - A navigation_expression receiver is handled ONLY when rooted at 'this' (Case 1b). Otherwise nothing is emitted: the unresolved-edge fallback ('if not edge_added', ~1740) lives inside the final else branch, which a nav receiver never enters.\n   - Any other receiver node type (string_literal, parenthesized_expression, index_expression, super_expression, number literal, ...) is skipped. The METHOD identifier is then taken as the receiver, method_node stays None, and no edge is emitted.\n   The earlier guess ('a navigation chain of identifiers with no import binding') was wrong: import binding is not the variable.\n\n3. THE FAMILY, shipped survey (scratchpad dupol/chain, dupol/recv). NO calls edge for:\n     h.file.readText()   (TYPED field chain; the receiver is java.io.File)\n     System.out.println(\"x\")\n     h.name.trim()\n     \"x\".trim()\n     (f).readText()\n     fs[0].readText()\n     super.go()   (an in-repo override calling its base)\n   Emitted as controls: f.readText(), System.getenv(\"K\"), File(p).readText().\n\n4. SIZE. This is a tree-sitter census of receiver node types, NOT the instrument; it reads the analyzer's loop, not its output.\n   okhttp, 462 .kt files, 51,099 call_expressions:\n     nav receiver not rooted at 'this'  1,585\n     string literal                       908\n     unary                                459\n     multiline string                     138\n     parenthesized                         74\n     super                                 64\n     number                                63\n     index                                 35\n     other                                 21\n     TOTAL                              3,347  (6.5%)\n   detekt-core: 64 nav receivers of 3,455 calls.\n   Inline fully-qualified java/javax static calls, the filed instance, are RARE: 53 sites across 5,052 .kt files in ~/ALL_REPOS. Of those, I/O-relevant: Files.createTempDirectory 1, LocalDate.now 8, System clock reads 2.\n   NOT checked: whether the unary count is a grammar artifact (e.g. '!x.m()' parsing with the unary as the receiver); read a sample before citing it.\n\n5. PRIOR ART: WI-nasuf (done) fixed the identifier and call_expression receiver arms; INV-bamij covered package-level anchoring. Neither covers these receiver shapes. The statement is INV-foluz's ('every call site ... produces a call edge'), in kotlin.\n\nTitle, statement and root_cause updated to the family. The fq-inline form stays the filed instance. Priority unchanged."  # 1b9e
